# .gitignore — The Emperor's Inner Canon
#
# This is a video-content-production repository. What belongs in git:
# production documents (markdown), character style-key art (assets/*.png).
# What does not: the rendered
# video/audio those documents describe, and anything machine-local.

# ── Generated / downloaded media ─────────────────────────────
# Final MP4s from Higgsfield are CDN downloads archived locally, never
# committed — a single longform episode can run to hundreds of megabytes
# and would live in the history forever.
# Convention: download renders into output/<book>/ch<N>/renders/
renders/
*.mp4
*.mov
*.webm
*.mkv
*.wav
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.aac
# Subtitle sidecars (.srt/.vtt) are small text and are required
# deliverables — intentionally NOT ignored.
# To commit a media file anyway: git add -f <path>

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Higgsfield / generation-service tokens must never be committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ── Node (scripts/) ──────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.npm/

# ── Office lock & temp files ────────────────────────
~$*
*.tmp

# ── Claude Code local overrides ──────────────────────────────
# .claude/settings.json is tracked; per-machine overrides are not.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.json

# ── Scratch / work-in-progress ───────────────────────────────
scratch/
_wip/
*.bak

# ── OS & editor cruft ────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
